          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:70226e6590ce8e3668704a6cf8422f99c91651fd5fcf0ed35f9712b9b5107742:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_feb5066e65f74d09a0c2e0e6ed653c35",
      "statement": "The orchestrator's _monitor streams the runner's stdout (stderr merged) line by line into the per-run log file <data>/logs/run-<id>.log (buffering lines until the runner creates its Run row, then flushing and recording log_path on the row), pushes lines to registered UI log subscribers, keeps the last 100 lines in memory for Run.notes, and in its finally block releases the process/monitor tracking entries and the global semaphore.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://apps/billcollector/orchestrator.py#L360-L433",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1b273216d703f62ae3a3ad6b674e77aef511301bc971fba335a076c00ccae789:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f907f976506b496eac8eb747109362b5",
      "statement": "The orchestrator's _finalize_run only closes Run rows the runner left open (result IS NULL), mapping exit 0 to success, a negative (signal-killed) exit to interrupted, and any other non-zero exit to failure while setting ended_at and releasing the task to idle; on a real non-zero exit it appends the output tail to Run.notes, and when the runner exited before creating a Run row it only releases the task claim.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://apps/billcollector/orchestrator.py#L435-L476",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ef03d6925c1cb45ba0f6396298fdf3b150833332d80fd1fe67ed4a333662c57f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0f2699ba63254543ad3343f203bb0da0",
      "statement": "Orchestrator.cleanup_orphans (the serve startup hook) marks every active Run row (result IS NULL) whose runner pid is dead or unrecorded as interrupted, force-removes its stale display lock, and releases the task to idle; a run whose pid is still alive is left alone so its orphaned runner can finalize itself.",
      "evidence": [
