      "statement": "Orchestrator.shutdown SIGTERMs every live runner's whole process group, SIGKILLs after SHUTDOWN_TIMEOUT (5 s), marks still-open Run rows as interrupted, releases tasks, and awaits the monitors; stop_run (UI Stop) signals only one task's runner group (SIGKILL after STOP_TIMEOUT 10 s) and never touches the Run row, leaving finalization to the runner's signal handler or monitor.",
