    {
      "id": "claim_5d9d5c7e4c8f4bc19cce3cb38b7d9777",
      "statement": "There are exactly three pause entry points in the runner: _execute_step_with_pause (reason step_failed, after a non-graceful step exhausts its attempts), _handle_download_with_pause (reason download_failed), and _execute_wait_user_step (reason wait_user, pausing before execution and consuming the step on resume); all call pause_loop, which persists the machine-readable context on the Run row, flips the task to 'waiting' so the scheduler's row lock cannot re-trigger it, pushes an ntfy deep link, and blocks on the versioned control socket until resume (re-executes the step with a fresh attempt budget), cancel, or the pause_deadline_seconds deadline is exceeded.",
