    {
      "id": "claim_a6dc3853958047eda8e32a7a4b3293bf",
      "statement": "Display allocation is runner-owned: allocate_display claims the next free Xvfb display in the configured range (display_start .. display_start+display_count-1, defaults :99 with 16 displays) via an atomic O_EXCL lockfile under data/displays/ (websockify port 6080+offset, x11vnc RFB port 5900+display); release_display is PID-checked, and the stack children (Xvfb, x11vnc, websockify) stay in the runner's process group so a daemon-shutdown group signal tears the stack down with the runner.",
