    {
      "id": "claim_f3d50a5338eb4953b2f99b32d6c2328f",
      "statement": "The runner installs SIGTERM/SIGINT handlers that raise RunInterrupted in the main thread so a shutdown takes the run's full teardown (display reap, claim release, Run finalization); a signal after the Run row exists ends the run result=interrupted, while a signal before the row exists exits 1 with the orchestrator's no-row path releasing the claim; every best-effort except-Exception handler on the run path re-raises RunInterrupted.",
